  "title": "Partitionning a tournament into k-strongly connected subtournaments.",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Problem Let $k_1, \\dots, k_p$ be positve integer Does there exists an integer $g(k_1, \\dots, k_p)$ such that every $g(k_1, \\dots, k_p)$-strong tournament $T$ admits a partition $(V_1\\dots, V_p)$ of its vertex set such that the subtournament induced by $V_i$ is a non-trivial $k_i$-strong for all $1\\leq i\\leq p$.",
